{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DeferredTask","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Success","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Success","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"DeferredTask","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" represents an asynchronous operation that is defined but does not start executing until it is explicitly started.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This allows precise control over when the asynchronous work begins, supporting scenarios where you want to set up an async operation ahead of time and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trigger its execution at a chosen moment.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This type conforms to the "},{"code":"AsynchronousUnitOfWork","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol and is useful for wrapping async computations, network requests, or any other asynchronous operation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that may throw an error and returns a value."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Example","anchor":"Example","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Basic usage with ","type":"text"},{"code":"execute()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to start and await the operation:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let deferred = DeferredTask<Int> {","    try await Task.sleep(nanoseconds: 1_000_000_000)","    return 42","}","let result = try await deferred.execute()","print(\"Result is \\(result)\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Accessing the result via the "},{"code":"result","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property (an async property that awaits completion):"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let deferred = DeferredTask<Int> {","    10 * 5","}","let value = await deferred.result","print(\"Value is \\(value)\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Running the operation without awaiting its result immediately, via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run()"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let deferred = DeferredTask<Int> {","    7 + 3","}","deferred.run()","\/\/ Later, you may await the result property or handle completion otherwise"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Subscribing to the task’s events using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subscribe()"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let deferred = DeferredTask<String> {","    \"Hello, World!\"","}","let cancellable = deferred.subscribe { event in","    switch event {","    case .success(let value):","        print(\"Completed with value: \\(value)\")","    case .failure(let error):","        print(\"Failed with error: \\(error)\")","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storing the subscription in a collection for lifecycle management:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var cancellables = Set<AnyCancellable>()","let deferred = DeferredTask<Void> {","    print(\"Task executed\")","}","deferred.subscribe().store(in: &cancellables)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Chaining with operators:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let result = try await DeferredTask { 21 }","    .map { $0 * 2 }","    .execute() \/\/ result is 42"],"type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Aflue